Algorithm Logic

Start from a selected vertex.

Recursively select an adjacent vertex that has not already been visited.

When all vertices have been visited, verify whether the final vertex connects back to the starting vertex.

Display the pseudocode:

text
Hamiltonian(path, position):
    if position == V:
        return edge(path[V-1], path[0]) exists

    for each vertex v:
        if isSafe(v, path, position):
            path[position] = v

            if Hamiltonian(path, position + 1):
                return true

            path[position] = -1

    return false


