Branch and Bound Implementation

Use a valid lower-bound calculation for the symmetric TSP.

For example, use the sum of the minimum incident edge requirements for unvisited vertices and current path endpoints, adjusted appropriately to produce an admissible lower bound.

Alternatively, use a clearly explained MST-based lower bound:

Current path cost + MST cost of remaining vertices + minimum connection from the current endpoint to the remaining set + minimum connection from the remaining set back to the start.

Handle special cases where no feasible connection exists.

Use the lower bound to prune branches whose best possible completion cannot improve the current best complete tour.

Explain:

State-space tree.
Partial route construction.
Current route cost.
Lower-bound calculation.
Incumbent or best-known complete solution.
Branch expansion.
Pruning.
Optimal route reconstruction.

Display pseudocode:

text
BranchAndBoundTSP():
    initialize priority queue
    create initial state
    calculate initial lower bound
    insert initial state

    while queue is not empty:
        state = remove state with smallest bound

        if state.bound >= bestCost:
            prune state
            continue

        for each unvisited city:
            create child state
            update route cost
            calculate child lower bound

            if child is complete:
                update best solution if better
            else if child.bound < bestCost:
                insert child into queue


Display complexity:

Worst-case time complexity: O(n!).
Space complexity: O(n!) in the worst case for the priority queue and search states.

