Branch and Bound Algorithm

Use a fractional-knapsack upper bound to estimate the maximum possible return from a partial selection.

Sort items by decreasing value-to-weight ratio.

For each state, calculate:

Current project level.
Current total investment.
Current total return.
Upper bound on achievable return.

The upper bound may include fractional selection of the next project, even though the final solution must select projects entirely or not at all.

Prune any state whose upper bound cannot exceed the best complete solution already found.

Display pseudocode:

text
BranchAndBoundKnapsack():
    sort projects by value / cost ratio

    create root node
    calculate root upper bound
    insert root into priority queue

    while queue is not empty:
        node = remove node with highest upper bound

        if node.bound <= bestReturn:
            prune node
            continue

        create include-project child

        if child.weight <= budget:
            update best solution if better
            calculate upper bound
            insert child if promising

        create exclude-project child
        calculate upper bound

        insert child if its bound can improve bestReturn


